(window.AeroSenseTranslations ||= []).push({"A fly-brain route from curiosity to understanding.":"循著果蠅腦的路徑，從好奇走向理解。","Why education belongs in the project":"為什麼教育是專案的一部分","A fact can be understood.":"知識可以被理解。","A decision has to be practised.":"決策則需要練習。","Education is a right, and a way for people to take part in decisions that affect them. Article 26 of the Universal Declaration of Human Rights and SDG 4 give that commitment a public foundation; Target 4.7 connects learning to sustainable development. For AeroSense, it means making the science accessible enough to question, use and eventually build on.":"教育是一項權利，也讓人們能參與影響自己的決策。《世界人權宣言》第 26 條與 SDG 4，為這份承諾提供公共基礎；目標 4.7 則將學習與永續發展相連。對 AeroSense 而言，這代表要讓科學容易理解，使人能夠提問、運用，並最終在其基礎上繼續建構。","Our initial survey changed the question we wanted to ask. Explaining that mold can be dangerous was too broad. Our working summary pointed instead to decisions people make about heat, smell and visible spoilage. We therefore built opportunities to choose an answer, see why it matters and try a new situation. The team now reports 107 responses; item-level counts still need verification, so this page does not turn the early summary into population percentages.":"初期問卷改變了我們想問的問題。只解釋黴菌可能有危險，範圍太廣；工作摘要反而指向人們對加熱、氣味與可見腐敗所做的決策。因此，我們設計讓人選擇答案、理解其重要性，再嘗試新情境的機會。團隊目前回報 107 份回覆，但逐題人數仍待核實，因此本頁不會把早期摘要轉換成人口比例。","Active participation gave us a useful starting point. Freeman and colleagues' synthesis of 225 undergraduate STEM studies found an average 0.47-standard-deviation improvement in examination performance with active learning. Wouters and colleagues found benefits of serious games for learning and retention, with no clear overall motivation advantage. Those results justify testing an approach; they do not establish that our own games work.":"主動參與提供了有用的起點。Freeman 與同事綜整 225 項大學 STEM 研究，發現主動學習平均使考試表現提升 0.47 個標準差。Wouters 與同事發現嚴肅遊戲有助於學習與保留，但整體動機優勢並不明確。這些結果支持我們測試此方法，卻不能證明我們自己的遊戲有效。","We also wanted a conversation about synthetic biology itself. What does it mean to put a fruit-fly odor receptor into cultured HEK293 cells? What can a fluorescent response tell us? Who should act on a screening result? Each activity below gives a different audience a way into those questions.":"我們也希望開啟關於合成生物學本身的對話。把果蠅氣味受體放進培養的 HEK293 細胞，代表什麼？螢光反應能告訴我們什麼？誰應該依據篩檢結果採取行動？下方每項活動，都為不同觀眾提供進入這些問題的方式。","Our education journey · a fly-brain map":"我們的教育旅程 · 果蠅腦地圖","The route borrows three landmarks from the fly olfactory system: sensory input reaches the antennal lobe, projection neurons carry information toward the mushroom-body calyx, and mushroom-body output pathways link learned information to behaviour. We use that route as an educational metaphor for first contact, deeper understanding and sharing what has been learned. The biological circuit has feedback and parallel pathways; the map is a reading guide.":"這條路線借用果蠅嗅覺系統的三個地標：感覺輸入到達觸角葉，投射神經元將資訊送往蘑菇體萼部，蘑菇體輸出路徑則將學到的資訊連結至行為。我們用這條路徑作為初次接觸、深入理解與分享所學的教育比喻。生物迴路存在回饋與平行路徑；這張地圖是閱讀指南。","01 · Antennal lobe":"01 · 觸角葉","First contact":"初次接觸","Survey, three games and social media: find the question that gets someone to stop and think.":"問卷、三款遊戲與社群媒體：找到讓人停下來思考的問題。","Enter the input stage ↗":"進入輸入階段 ↗","02 · Mushroom-body calyx":"02 · 蘑菇體萼部","Build understanding":"建立理解","Connect biology, measurement and interpretation through a curriculum and guided learning.":"透過課程與引導式學習，連結生物學、量測與解讀。","Enter the learning stage ↗":"進入學習階段 ↗","03 · Mushroom-body output":"03 · 蘑菇體輸出","Take it into a room":"把知識帶進新的場合","Explain the work to new audiences, exchange questions and leave resources others can reuse.":"向新觀眾解釋研究、交流問題，並留下可供他人重用的資源。","Enter the exchange stage ↗":"進入交流階段 ↗","Region 01 · Antennal lobe / input":"區域 01 · 觸角葉／輸入","Olfactory signals first converge in the antennal lobe. Our first educational layer also brings many starting points together: a survey surfaces existing beliefs, a game makes a pattern tangible, and a social post reaches a person who was not looking for a science lesson.":"嗅覺訊號首先在觸角葉匯聚。我們的第一層教育也匯集多種起點：問卷呈現既有觀念，遊戲讓模式變得具體，社群貼文則接觸原本沒有在找科學課程的人。","The survey gave us a question to work on.":"問卷給了我們一個可以著手的問題。","The diagnostic asked about food storage, visible mold, heating and the reliability of smell. We use it to identify concepts for discussion, rather than to label an audience as uninformed. Its educational role is to connect a familiar household decision to the limits of a signal: seeing or smelling one feature cannot answer every food-safety question.":"這份初步診斷詢問食品儲存、可見黴菌、加熱，以及氣味是否可靠。我們用它找出值得討論的概念，而不是把觀眾標籤為缺乏知識。它的教育角色，是將熟悉的家庭決策連結至訊號的限制：看見或聞到某一項特徵，無法回答所有食品安全問題。","Our response was a short decision exercise followed by an explanation and a chance to reconsider. The questions below are for the visitor; choices stay in this browser tab and do not add respondents to our study.":"我們的回應是簡短的決策練習，接著提供解釋與重新思考的機會。下方問題供訪客練習；選擇只留在此瀏覽器分頁，不會新增至研究受訪者名單。","28 responses informed the redesign; 107 is a later collection total.":"28 份回覆提供重新設計的依據；107 是後期蒐集總數。","The team’s engineering narrative cites the early questionnaire record on":"團隊的工程敘述引用了早期問卷記錄，日期為","23 August 2026":"2026 年 8 月 23 日",". Most respondents already rejected the three claims. We therefore replaced broad awareness messaging with decisions about heat, visible mold and sensory evidence. The date and item counts for the later 107-response collection have not been supplied; no result below is attributed to that larger denominator.":"。多數填答者原本就否定這三項說法，因此我們將廣泛的意識宣導，改為對加熱、可見黴菌與感官證據的決策練習。後期 107 份回覆的蒐集日期與逐題人數尚未提供；下列結果皆不歸屬於這個較大的分母。","Early diagnostic summary — n = 28; source-reported aggregate counts":"早期診斷摘要——n = 28；來源回報的彙整人數","Claim respondents correctly rejected":"填答者正確否定的說法","Correct rejection count":"正確否定人數","Share of early sample":"占早期樣本比例","Cutting off visible mold makes the rest safe":"切掉可見黴菌，剩下部分就安全","Heating or roasting fully eliminates mycotoxins":"加熱或烘烤會完全消除真菌毒素","Normal appearance and smell establish no risk":"外觀與氣味正常，就能確定沒有風險","Download the aggregate table (CSV)":"下載彙整表格（CSV）",". Percentages are calculated from the reported integers. The raw questionnaire export, coding file and missing-response breakdown are not available. This non-random, consumer-skewed sample informs what to teach; it is not a population estimate or a pre/post evaluation.":"。百分比由回報的整數人數計算。原始問卷匯出檔、編碼檔與缺答分布皆無法取得。這個非隨機且偏向消費者的樣本，用來決定教什麼；不是人口估計，也不是前後測評估。","Diagnosis":"診斷","This is not a data-collection form and not part of our research sample. Choices stay in this browser tab. They are not stored, sent, logged, or added to n = 107.":"這不是資料蒐集表單，也不屬於我們的研究樣本。選擇只留在此瀏覽器分頁，不會儲存、傳送、記錄或加進 n = 107。","Claim 1":"說法 1","Cutting off the visible mold makes the rest safe to eat.":"切掉看得見的黴菌後，剩下的部分就可以安全食用。","Do you agree or disagree with this statement?":"你同意還是不同意這個說法？","Agree":"同意","Disagree":"不同意","Scientific interpretation":"科學解讀","Disagree. Removing a visible colony does not automatically make the rest of a food safe. In some firm foods, public guidance allows cutting away a margin; in soft, moist, or porous foods, mycelium and some mycotoxins can extend beyond what you see. “Always safe” is the over-claim.":"不同意。去除可見菌落，不會自動讓食品剩餘部分變安全。某些質地堅實的食品，公共指引允許連同周圍一段範圍切除；但在柔軟、潮濕或多孔的食品中，菌絲與部分真菌毒素可能延伸至肉眼看不見的地方。「一律安全」是過度主張。","Claim 2":"說法 2","Heating or roasting fully eliminates mycotoxins.":"加熱或烘烤會完全消除真菌毒素。","Disagree. Heat may inactivate molds without eliminating heat-stable mycotoxins. Killing or reducing the organism is not the same as removing the metabolite. “Fully eliminates” is not a safe general rule for ordinary cooking.":"不同意。加熱可能使黴菌失活，卻未必消除耐熱的真菌毒素。殺死或減少生物，不等於移除其代謝物。對一般烹調而言，「完全消除」不是可放心通用的規則。","Claim 3":"說法 3","If it looks and smells normal, it’s not risky.":"只要外觀與氣味正常，就沒有風險。","Disagree. Appearance and smell cannot establish mycotoxin status. Absence of an off-odor does not prove absence of toxin; presence of mold does not by itself quantify a toxin. Sensory inspection is not an assay.":"不同意。外觀與氣味無法確立真菌毒素狀態。沒有異味，不能證明沒有毒素；有黴菌，也無法單憑這點定量毒素。感官檢查不是檢驗。","Survey data status":"問卷資料狀態","The early record contains 28 responses and three aggregate item counts. A later total of 107 is team reported; its item-level analysis has not been supplied.":"早期記錄包含 28 份回覆與三題彙整人數。後期總數 107 是團隊回報，尚未提供逐題分析。","Limitation":"限制","An initial diagnostic, not a population estimate.":"這是初步診斷，不是人口估計。","The design decision rests on the early n = 28 summary, not the later n = 107 total. Neither stage supports population prevalence or learning gain.":"設計決策依據的是早期 n = 28 摘要，而不是後期 n = 107 總數。兩個階段都不支持推論人口盛行比例或學習增益。","Non-random sample. People were not drawn with a sampling frame that supports inference beyond this group.":"非隨機樣本。參與者並非透過可支持推論至此群體之外的抽樣架構選出。","We used this to choose":"我們用這份資料選擇","what to teach":"要教什麼",". We do not use it to estimate how common these beliefs are in the public.":"，不以此估計這些觀念在大眾中有多普遍。","Scientific readings":"科學解讀","The interactive choices require JavaScript. The 107-response survey's item-level results are pending verification.":"互動選項需要 JavaScript。107 份問卷的逐題結果尚待核實。","Removing visible mold does not automatically make every food safe.":"去除可見黴菌，不會自動讓每一種食品都變安全。","Ordinary cooking does not guarantee removal of all mycotoxins.":"一般烹調不能保證移除所有真菌毒素。","Appearance and smell do not establish toxin status.":"外觀與氣味無法確立毒素狀態。","Online games · Odor Pixel Suite":"線上遊戲 · 氣味像素遊戲套組","A smell is a pattern across channels. That sentence is easier to understand after a pattern has fooled you. Our three browser games turn recognition, navigation and mixture decoding into decisions a player can try. They are simplified teaching models, with formal learning evaluation still pending.":"氣味是跨通道的模式。當你曾被一組模式誤導過，這句話就更容易理解。我們的三款瀏覽器遊戲，將辨識、導航與混合物解碼轉成玩家能嘗試的決策。它們是簡化教學模型，正式學習評估仍待進行。","01 · Recognise":"01 · 辨識","Odor Pixel Lab":"氣味像素實驗室","Match an odor to a pattern of receptor-like signals, including patterns with noise. The question is how identity survives imperfect measurements.":"將氣味對應至類受體訊號模式，也包含有雜訊的模式。問題在於：量測不完美時，氣味身分如何仍可辨識？","Play the pattern game ↗":"玩模式遊戲 ↗","02 · Navigate":"02 · 導航","Odor Maze":"氣味迷宮","(Scentbound Labyrinth)":"（Scentbound Labyrinth）","Explore a maze and use scent information unlocked along the route. The activity makes a signal useful through the choice it helps a player make.":"探索迷宮，使用沿途解鎖的氣味資訊。這項活動透過訊號幫助玩家做出的選擇，展現訊號的用途。","Enter the maze ↗":"進入迷宮 ↗","03 · Decode":"03 · 解碼","Odor Fingerprint Mixer":"氣味指紋混合器","Explore overlapping patterns from odor mixtures. A mixed fingerprint is an interpretation problem, which connects the activity to AeroSense's decoding layer.":"探索氣味混合物形成的重疊模式。混合指紋是一個解讀問題，也讓活動連結到 AeroSense 的解碼層。","Explore the mixer ↗":"探索混合器 ↗","Open the complete bilingual suite":"開啟完整雙語遊戲套組",". Educators can use the":"。教育工作者可以使用","optional study protocol":"選用研究流程","to pair responses. Casual visitors can start playing immediately.":"來配對回覆。一般訪客則可直接開始遊玩。","Three formats for a scrolling audience.":"為滑動瀏覽的觀眾設計三種形式。","The survey and the games ask people to seek us out. Instagram lets us introduce the same ideas in a feed they already use. We separated that work into technical carousels, sustainability questions and short explanations, each with a different job.":"問卷與遊戲需要人們主動找到我們。Instagram 則讓我們在他們原本就使用的動態消息中介紹相同概念。我們將這項工作分成技術輪播圖、永續提問與簡短解說，各自承擔不同任務。","From a fly nose to an edge device":"從果蠅的鼻子，到邊緣裝置","The first carousel asks, “What if we put a fruit fly's nose inside a human cell?” It explains the intended chain from odor recognition through calcium to a fluorescent reporter. The two published teaching graphics below make the receptor and reporter visible. Fluorescence in our experimental system still needs to be characterised against controls; brightness alone is not a calibrated odor-concentration scale.":"第一組輪播圖問：「如果把果蠅的鼻子放進人類細胞呢？」內容說明從氣味辨識、鈣離子到螢光報導蛋白的預定鏈結。下方兩張已發布的教學圖，讓受體與報導蛋白變得可見。我們實驗系統中的螢光仍需與對照比較分析；單看亮度，不是經校正的氣味濃度尺度。","Parts Design · an entry point into the living-sensor idea.":"元件設計 · 進入活體感測器概念的起點。","Parts Design · connecting molecular components to the intended signal.":"元件設計 · 將分子元件連結至預期訊號。","The two published Parts Design graphics are the current technical series.":"目前的技術系列，是兩張已發布的元件設計圖。","covers the decoding and reader carousels and short science videos.":"涵蓋解碼與讀取器輪播圖，以及科學短影片。","Sustainability Pop Quiz":"永續小測驗","Four question-and-answer cards connect a design choice with an SDG. Open a card below to see the intended connection.":"四張問答卡片，將設計選擇連結至 SDG。開啟下方卡片，查看預期的連結。","Earlier warning of disease in a fruit shipment?":"更早對水果貨運中的病害提出警訊？","SDG 2 · Zero Hunger.":"SDG 2 · 消除飢餓。","The intended benefit is more time to decide what to do with a batch. Detection lead time and avoided loss still need measurement.":"預期效益是增加決定如何處理批次的時間。偵測提前量與避免的損失仍需量測。","A biological sensor with a custom optical reader?":"生物感測器搭配客製化光學讀取器？","SDG 9 · Industry, Innovation and Infrastructure.":"SDG 9 · 產業、創新與基礎設施。","Building local research and engineering capability. The integrated platform's performance and power are validation questions.":"建立在地研究與工程能力。整合平台的效能與功耗仍是待驗證問題。","A cartridge designed for repeated readings?":"為重複讀取而設計的匣體？","SDG 12 · Responsible Consumption and Production.":"SDG 12 · 責任消費與生產。","Reuse is a design aim. Lifetime tests and a life-cycle comparison must establish any reduction in waste.":"重用是一項設計目標。是否減少廢棄物，必須透過壽命測試與生命週期比較確認。","Design choices changed by people outside the lab?":"實驗室以外的人，改變了設計選擇？","SDG 17 · Partnerships for the Goals.":"SDG 17 · 夥伴關係。","Knowledge-sharing can improve a design. An interview, mentorship and a formal partnership describe different relationships.":"知識共享能改善設計。訪談、導師指導與正式合作，描述的是不同關係。","We will evaluate this channel as reach and dialogue: what people save, ask or challenge. Those observations will inform future posts. Learning change needs a separate before-and-after assessment, so follower activity is not reported as a learning gain.":"我們會從觸及與對話評估此管道：人們收藏、提問或質疑了什麼。這些觀察將引導未來貼文。學習改變需要另行進行前後評估，因此不把追蹤者活動當作學習增益。","Region 02 · Mushroom-body calyx / integration":"區域 02 · 蘑菇體萼部／整合","At the mushroom-body calyx, projection-neuron input reaches Kenyon cells. Our second educational layer connects ideas that first arrived separately: how a receptor works, why a reader needs controls, and how an algorithm can turn patterns into a decision.":"在蘑菇體萼部，投射神經元的輸入到達 Kenyon 細胞。我們的第二層教育連結最初分別接觸的概念：受體如何運作、讀取器為何需要對照，以及演算法如何把模式轉為決策。","The self-paced curriculum follows one odor signal across the project. Five modules use a question, an explanation, an interactive activity and a short assessment to connect the next concept. Learners can start with any module and revisit their browser-local progress.":"自訂進度課程沿著同一個氣味訊號，走過整個專案。五個模組以提問、解釋、互動活動與短評量，逐步連結下一個概念。學習者可以從任何模組開始，也能回顧保存在自己瀏覽器的進度。","01 · Discover":"01 · 發現","From volatile molecules to receptor patterns.":"從揮發性分子，到受體模式。","02 · Question":"02 · 提問","Can a smell answer a safety question?":"氣味能回答安全問題嗎？","Practise the limits of heat, appearance and odor as evidence.":"練習辨認加熱、外觀與氣味作為證據的限制。","03 · Build":"03 · 建構","How could a cell become a sensor?":"細胞如何成為感測器？","Connect receptor, reporter and measurement.":"連結受體、報導蛋白與量測。","04 · Decode":"04 · 解碼","What does the pattern mean?":"這個模式代表什麼？","Use the fly circuit as an entry point into computational interpretation.":"以果蠅迴路作為理解運算解讀的起點。","05 · Decide":"05 · 決定","What should happen next?":"接下來應該怎麼做？","Use uncertainty, screening and confirmation to choose a responsible action.":"運用不確定性、篩檢與確認，選擇負責任的行動。","Enter the Learning Lab ↗":"進入學習實驗室 ↗","The modules and their assessment instruments are available now. A visitor's saved score is personal feedback; it is not automatically collected into a research dataset. Formal cohort outcomes remain to be evaluated.":"模組與評量工具目前已可使用。訪客儲存的分數是個人回饋，不會自動蒐集成研究資料集。正式群體學習成果仍待評估。","Region 03 · Mushroom-body output / exchange":"區域 03 · 蘑菇體輸出／交流","The last part of this map is about taking an explanation into a new setting. Industry visitors, neuroscience students and other iGEM teams bring different assumptions. Their questions reveal which links in our story need more work. The events below document that exchange; they are not controlled learning trials.":"地圖的最後一部分，是將解釋帶入新的場合。產業訪客、神經科學學生與其他 iGEM 團隊，都帶著不同假設。他們的問題，讓我們知道故事中的哪些連結仍需加強。下方活動記錄的是這些交流，不是受控學習試驗。","May 2026 · SynBioBeta":"2026 年 5 月 · SynBioBeta","Explaining the platform beyond our own university":"向大學以外的觀眾解釋平台","We presented AeroSense in the NextGen Bioleader / poster setting at SynBioBeta 2026. The audience included people working in industry and synthetic biology, so we had to explain where biology, optics and computation meet before discussing technical detail. The event tested how the platform reads to people who do not share our lab's starting assumptions.":"我們在 SynBioBeta 2026 的 NextGen Bioleader／海報場合展示 AeroSense。觀眾包括產業與合成生物學工作者，因此在討論技術細節前，必須先解釋生物、光學與運算的交會處。這項活動讓我們檢視，不共享實驗室起始假設的人會如何理解平台。","Taking AeroSense's platform story to SynBioBeta 2026.":"將 AeroSense 的平台故事帶到 SynBioBeta 2026。","The same team event photograph appears in Human Practices.":"同一張團隊活動照片也出現在人文實踐頁面。","A new audience for the same scientific question.":"同一個科學問題，面對新的觀眾。","Read our conference poster (PDF) ↗":"閱讀研討會海報（PDF）↗","September 2026 · China Medical University":"2026 年 9 月 · 中國醫藥大學","Start with the biology, then connect the engineering.":"先從生物學開始，再連結工程。","At Prof. Ching-Che Charng's home institution, we shared AeroSense in a neuroscience course. The session introduced synthetic biology, iGEM and the project to students whose background was closer to neuroscience than to synthetic-biology engineering. That changed our explanation: begin with the odor-sensing logic, then show why the receptor, reporter and reader each have a distinct job.":"我們在 Ching-Che Charng 教授任職學校的神經科學課程分享 AeroSense。活動向背景較接近神經科學、而非合成生物學工程的學生，介紹合成生物學、iGEM 與專案。這改變了說明方式：先談氣味感測邏輯，再展示受體、報導蛋白與讀取器為何各有不同任務。","Sharing the project in a neuroscience classroom.":"在神經科學課堂分享專案。","The same visit photograph appears in Human Practices.":"同一張參訪照片也出現在人文實踐頁面。","Discussion helped us practise a more accessible biological explanation.":"討論幫助我們練習更容易理解的生物學說明。","October 2026 · iGEM TAU":"2026 年 10 月 · iGEM TAU","Different teams, different ways to tell a research story.":"不同團隊，以不同方式講述研究故事。","We took part in the 2026 iGEM Teams Meetup organised by Tel Aviv University's iGEM team. Teams from the Americas, Europe and Asia explained their work in different ways. The exchange gave us another audience for our project and a chance to compare how teams connect a problem, a design and a claim.":"我們參加由特拉維夫大學 iGEM 團隊主辦的 2026 iGEM Teams Meetup。來自美洲、歐洲與亞洲的團隊，以不同方式介紹研究。這場交流為專案帶來另一群觀眾，也讓我們比較各團隊如何連結問題、設計與主張。","Reusable now · teacher packet in preparation":"目前可重用 · 教師教材包準備中","Leave an activity someone else can run.":"留下別人也能帶領的活動。","The Learning Lab, games and educator protocol provide the current reusable materials. The planned teacher toolkit will bring a lesson guide, slides and worksheets together in one packet. Until that packet is complete, the links below point to the resources that already exist.":"學習實驗室、遊戲與教育者流程，是目前可重用的教材。規劃中的教師工具包，將整合教案、投影片與學習單。在套件完成前，下方連結先提供已存在的資源。","Use the teaching resources ↗":"使用教學資源 ↗","What we can learn from the next round":"下一輪能學到什麼","We have built activities, published teaching content and taken the project into new settings. The next question is what a learner can explain or decide afterward. We will score only paired responses from the same anonymous participant, report missing responses and keep age groups and instruments separate. A new transfer question will help distinguish remembering an answer from applying an idea.":"我們已建立活動、發布教學內容，並將專案帶入新場合。下一個問題是：學習者之後能解釋或決定什麼？我們只計分同一匿名參與者的配對回覆，報告缺答情形，並將年齡組別與評量工具分開。新的遷移應用題，將幫助區分記住答案與運用概念。","Three kinds of evidence answer different questions: participation tells us who took part, discussion tells us what people asked, and a matched assessment can show what changed. We will use them together without converting one into another.":"三種證據回答不同問題：參與記錄說明誰曾參與，討論說明人們問了什麼，配對評量則可顯示改變了什麼。我們會共同使用三者，但不把其中一種轉換成另一種。","What each activity is intended to teach":"每項活動預期教會什麼","Learning objectives mapped to lesson and game activities, proposed assessment items and the available evidence. Published learning materials are distinguished from completed participant assessment; no paired-cohort learning gain is claimed.":"將學習目標對應至課程與遊戲活動、提議的評量題目，以及現有證據。已發布教材與已完成的參與者評量分開呈現；未宣稱有配對群體的學習增益。","Learning objective":"學習目標","Activity / mechanic":"活動／機制","Assessment":"評量","Evidence and limitation":"證據與限制","Explain odor as a pattern across channels":"解釋氣味是跨通道模式","Module 1":"模組 1","pattern matching under noise":"雜訊下的模式配對","Module pre/post questions; game concept and transfer items":"模組前後測題目；遊戲概念題與遷移應用題","Lesson and game available; no completed paired cohort":"課程與遊戲可使用；無已完成的配對群體","Distinguish visible mold, heat treatment and toxin evidence":"區分可見黴菌、熱處理與毒素證據","Module 2":"模組 2","; household decision exercise":"；家庭決策練習","Early n = 28 summary informed content; no measured learning gain":"早期 n = 28 摘要引導內容；未量測學習增益","Separate receptor expression, reporter activity and a valid measurement":"區分受體表現、報導蛋白活動與有效量測","Module 3":"模組 3","; connect components":"；連結元件","Module pre/post and reflection":"模組前後測與反思","Published instrument; no scored cohort":"已發布評量工具；無已評分群體","Interpret a pattern without assuming perfect classification":"解讀模式，同時避免假設分類完美無誤","Module 4":"模組 4","overlapping mixtures":"重疊混合物","Module pre/post; game transfer question":"模組前後測；遊戲遷移應用題","Simplified teaching model; not a sensor-validation experiment":"簡化教學模型，不是感測器驗證實驗","Use uncertainty to choose a next action":"運用不確定性選擇下一步行動","Module 5":"模組 5","screening and confirmation decisions":"篩檢與確認決策","Module pre/post and separate reflection":"模組前後測與獨立反思","Available to try; no participant feedback export or real-world decision outcome":"可供體驗；無參與者回饋匯出檔或實際決策結果","Use limited scent information to choose a route":"利用有限氣味資訊選擇路徑","Odor Maze (Scentbound Labyrinth)":"氣味迷宮（Scentbound Labyrinth）",": find the exit; chests unlock scans, guidance and secret passages":"：找到出口；寶箱解鎖掃描、引導與秘密通道","No version-matched Maze assessment supplied; archived QC Shift G2 items do not measure this objective":"尚未提供與版本相符的迷宮評量；封存的 QC Shift G2 題目不量測此目標","Current maze is playable; no evaluated cohort or measured learning effect":"目前迷宮可遊玩；無已評估群體或實測學習效果","Matched pre/post results require the same anonymous session and instrument. We keep the food-safety items separate from olfactory-coding game scores; a shared topic does not make their scales interchangeable.":"配對前後測結果，需要同一匿名工作階段與評量工具。我們將食品安全題目與嗅覺編碼遊戲分數分開；主題相同，不代表量尺可以互換。","Playtest record":"遊玩測試記錄","No completed playtest session log or participant export has been supplied. The":"尚未提供已完成的遊玩測試場次記錄或參與者匯出檔。","existing playtest protocol":"既有遊玩測試流程","defines the next study. A report will include date, audience, game version, completed and paired counts, missing responses, observed problems and resulting revisions. Empty fields are not zero participants.":"定義下一次研究。報告將包含日期、觀眾、遊戲版本、完成人數與配對人數、缺答情形、觀察到的問題與後續修訂。空白欄位不等於零位參與者。","A live resource is evidence that something was built. It is not automatically evidence that learning improved.":"資源已上線，證明有人完成了建構，卻不會自動證明學習有所改善。","Learning, dialogue, and reach answer different questions. They are never added into one “impact” score.":"學習、對話與觸及回答不同問題，絕不加總成單一「影響力」分數。","Delivery status is not evaluation status. Color is not the only indicator.":"交付狀態不等於評估狀態；顏色也不是唯一指標。","Instrument":"工具","Delivery":"交付","Evaluation":"評估","Initial survey":"初期問卷","Early summary available":"可取得早期摘要","— raw export and updated analysis unavailable":"——無原始匯出檔與更新分析","Diagnostic only —":"僅供診斷——","counts & caveats":"人數與注意事項","Odor Pixel Suite":"氣味像素遊戲套組","Live":"已上線","Evaluation pending":"評估待進行","Playable is not educational effectiveness.":"可遊玩不等於具教育成效。","A live course is not a cohort result.":"課程已上線不等於有群體成果。","University workshop":"大學工作坊","Not yet evaluated":"尚未評估","A planned session cannot yield outcomes.":"規劃中的活動不能產生成果。","Elementary-school camp":"國小營隊","Social media":"社群媒體","Reach is not learning. Figures not reported yet.":"觸及不等於學習；尚未報告數據。","A · Learning":"A · 學習","for paired gain. No empty bar charts and no fabricated zeros.":"的配對增益。不使用空白長條圖，也不捏造零值。","What exists today is a":"目前已有的是","diagnostic":"診斷","and a":"與","method":"方法",", not a gain table.":"，而不是增益表。","Available now.":"目前可取得。","Early 28-response aggregate summary":"早期 28 份回覆的彙整摘要","; later 107-response total with no supplied item-level analysis.":"；後期總數 107，未提供逐題分析。","Instrument context":"工具背景",". No learning gain is claimed.":"。未宣稱有學習增益。","Method ready, no cohort.":"方法已備妥，尚無群體。","Learning Lab same-item pre/post per module. Odor Pixel optional study mode with paired items, transfer items, and anonymous JSON/CSV export. Workshop/camp not yet run.":"學習實驗室各模組使用相同題目前後測。Odor Pixel 選用研究模式提供配對題目、遷移應用題，以及匿名 JSON／CSV 匯出。工作坊／營隊尚未舉辦。","Planned measure":"預定量測","Paired pre/post":"配對前後測","Unit":"單位","Individual item ID / paired participant when both scored answers exist":"個別題目 ID／同時有兩次有效計分答案時的配對參與者","Knowledge or decision change on those items, in percentage points":"這些題目上的知識或決策變化，以百分點表示","A short-term post-test does not establish long-term retention. Same-item tests can partly measure familiarity with the sentence.":"短期後測不能確立長期保留效果。相同題目測試可能部分量到的是對句子的熟悉度。","B · Dialogue":"B · 對話","Dialogue is participant questions, qualitative feedback, educator notes, or design suggestions that reached the team. Page views, clicks, likes, and game completion are not dialogue.":"對話是參與者的問題、質性回饋、教育者筆記，或傳達給團隊的設計建議。瀏覽量、點擊、按讚與遊戲完成次數不是對話。","No completed participant-feedback redesign cycle has yet been reported.":"尚未報告已完成的參與者回饋—重新設計循環。","No consented quotes, observation cards, or workshop notes are published.":"未公布經同意的引言、觀察卡或工作坊筆記。","University workshop and elementary camp are the planned dialogue settings.":"大學工作坊與國小營隊是規劃中的對話場合。","On-wiki discussion prompts are teaching aids, not a record of what anyone said.":"網站 上的討論提示是教學輔助，不是任何人發言的記錄。","C · Reach":"C · 觸及","Reach is not learning.":"觸及不等於學習。","Traffic is not knowledge gain.":"流量不等於知識增益。","Social Reach, Engagement, and Learning evidence:":"社群觸及、互動與學習證據：","Not reported yet":"尚未報告","— not zero.":"——並非零。","Game-visit analytics: not reported.":"遊戲造訪分析：未報告。","Resource downloads: no downloadable teacher file exists on this wiki yet, so no download count.":"資源下載：此 網站 尚無可下載的教師檔案，因此沒有下載次數。","Open access to the playable suite and the live Lab is a":"公開開放可遊玩的套組與已上線的學習實驗室，是","delivery":"交付","fact, not a participant count.":"事實，不是參與者人數。","Privacy: the Learning Lab and game study mode do not collect names, emails, or learner IDs. See":"隱私：學習實驗室與遊戲研究模式不蒐集姓名、電子郵件或學習者 ID。詳見","Safety · Data and privacy":"安全 · 資料與隱私","Assessment methods, instruments and reusable resources":"評量方法、工具與可重用資源","Food-safety decisions and olfactory / synthetic-biology literacy are different jobs. We reuse item IDs where the job is the same. We do not add the two chains into a single learning-gain number.":"食品安全決策與嗅覺／合成生物學素養，是不同的任務。任務相同時，我們重用題目 ID；不把兩條路徑加總為單一學習增益數字。","Each node is a delivery fact plus an evaluation fact. Evidence view (above) adds scanning labels. The path itself does not change.":"每個節點同時包含交付事實與評估事實。上方證據檢視增加了方便掃讀的標籤，路徑本身並未改變。","Chain A · Food-safety decision literacy":"路徑 A · 食品安全決策素養","Evidence available":"有可用證據","Reuse":"重用","Canonical item IDs":"標準題目 ID","A3 · Lab":"A3 · 學習實驗室","Learning Lab Module 2":"學習實驗室模組 2","Workshop / camp pre–post":"工作坊／營隊前後測","Dialogue":"對話","Paired outcome analysis":"配對成果分析","Bridge · AeroSense Learning Lab":"橋梁 · AeroSense 學習實驗室","Lab":"學習實驗室","One curriculum, two jobs":"一套課程，兩種任務","Module 2 feeds Chain A. Modules 1, 3, 4, and 5 feed Chain B. Do not pool those scores.":"模組 2 對應路徑 A；模組 1、3、4、5 對應路徑 B。不要合併這些分數。","Chain B · Olfaction and synthetic-biology literacy":"路徑 B · 嗅覺與合成生物學素養","B2 · Lab":"B2 · 學習實驗室","Modules 1, 3, 4, 5":"模組 1、3、4、5","Workshop / camp discussion":"工作坊／營隊討論","Conceptual / participation outcomes":"概念／參與成果","A1 · Initial survey":"A1 · 初期問卷","Audience":"對象","Delivery / Evaluation":"交付／評估","Completed · Evidence available (diagnostic only).":"已完成 · 有可用證據（僅供診斷）。","Survey status and sample caveats:":"問卷狀態與樣本注意事項：",". Storage / risk / trust modules:":"。儲存／風險／信任模組：","Survey instrument":"問卷工具","The same chains, as a list":"相同路徑的清單版本","This list is the complete method. The diagram above is a scanning aid. JavaScript is not required to read it.":"這份清單是完整方法。上方圖示僅協助掃讀，不需 JavaScript 也能閱讀。","A2 · Canonical misconception item IDs":"A2 · 標準迷思題目 ID","Educational question":"教育問題","Can later tools score the same three food-safety claims, so results can be compared?":"後續工具能否對相同三項食品安全說法計分，讓結果可以比較？","Instrument designers, educators, and future iGEM teams.":"評量工具設計者、教育工作者與未來 iGEM 團隊。","Instrument / activity":"工具／活動",", and":"，以及","in":"，位於","js/learning-data.js":"js/learning-data.js","What is measured":"量測什麼","Nothing by itself. This node is the shared schema that makes Chain A comparable across survey, Module 2, and a future workshop pre–post.":"本身不量測任何成果。此節點是共用綱要，讓問卷、模組 2 與未來工作坊前後測中的路徑 A 可以比較。","Live (source on this wiki)":"已上線（原始碼在此 網站）","Not yet evaluated as a cohort instrument":"尚未作為群體評量工具進行評估","Stable IDs and wording. No paired correction table.":"固定的 ID 與題目文字；無配對答題修正表。","Shared IDs enable comparability. They do not prove that learners changed. They are not used as Odor Pixel scores.":"共享 ID 讓結果可比較，但不能證明學習者改變了，也不作為 Odor Pixel 分數。","A3 · Learning Lab Module 2":"A3 · 學習實驗室模組 2","After a structured lesson, does a visitor reject the same three food-safety claims?":"完成有結構的課程後，訪客是否會否定相同三項食品安全說法？","Self-paced wiki visitors. No identified cohort.":"自訂進度的 網站 訪客，沒有已界定的群體。","Module 2 · If it looks fine, is it safe?":"模組 2 · 看起來沒問題，就安全嗎？","Same-item pre/post.":"相同題目前後測。","Change on the three canonical Chain A items, stored in this browser only.":"三項標準路徑 A 題目的變化，只儲存在此瀏覽器。","The live module and item IDs. No published class average.":"已上線模組與題目 ID；無已公布的班級平均值。","A live lesson is not a validated gain. Local scores are not a sample. Same-item pre/post can partly measure familiarity with the original wording.":"課程已上線不等於增益已驗證。本機分數不是研究樣本。相同題目前後測，可能部分量到對原始題目文字的熟悉程度。","A4 · Educator-mode / workshop / camp pre–post":"A4 · 教育者模式／工作坊／營隊前後測","Do facilitated audiences change on the same Chain A items when a teacher is in the room?":"在教師引導下，參與者對相同路徑 A 題目的回答是否改變？","Planned lower-year undergraduates; planned elementary-school camp. None published.":"規劃中的低年級大學生與國小營隊；皆未公布成果。","Module 2 and/or game educator-mode pre–post with anonymous export, once a session runs.":"活動執行後，使用模組 2 及／或遊戲教育者模式的前後測與匿名匯出。","Paired item-level correction on the canonical food-safety IDs, if that instrument is the one used in the room.":"若現場使用該工具，則量測標準食品安全 ID 的逐題配對答題修正。","None. Date, partner, and headcount are not inserted.":"無。不填入未取得的日期、夥伴與人數。","Educator-mode existing in a product is not a completed deployment. Game educator-mode is not automatically a Chain A instrument unless it uses these items.":"產品中有教育者模式，不代表已完成實際使用。遊戲教育者模式若未使用這些題目，就不會自動成為路徑 A 工具。","A5 · Paired outcome analysis":"A5 · 配對成果分析","Did the residual heat and look/smell habits actually move after teaching?":"教學之後，對加熱與外觀／氣味仍存的習慣是否真正改變？","A future consented cohort. None exists on this wiki.":"未來經同意的群體；此 網站 目前沒有。","Planned paired analysis of the canonical IDs. If collection permits, one parallel transfer item per concept (not yet written up as data).":"規劃對標準 ID 進行配對分析。若資料蒐集允許，每個概念另設一題平行遷移應用題（尚未作為資料發表）。","Pre/post change on Chain A claims. Transfer items, if added, would test generalization beyond the original sentence. No such results exist.":"路徑 A 說法的前後測變化。若加入遷移應用題，可測試是否能超越原始句子而泛化；目前沒有此類結果。","None. We do not invent paired rates.":"無。我們不捏造配對比例。","The analysis plan is not an outcome. Same-item gains can overstate learning if people only recognize the survey sentence.":"分析計畫不是成果。如果人們只是認出問卷句子，相同題目的增益可能高估學習。","Can one open curriculum serve both jobs without mixing their measurements?":"同一套開放課程，能否同時服務兩種任務，又不混合其量測？","Self-paced wiki visitors; future educators using on-wiki discussion prompts.":"自訂進度的 網站 訪客，以及未來使用 網站 討論提示的教育工作者。","Five-module":"五模組",". Module 2 = Chain A. Modules 1, 3, 4, 5 = Chain B.":"。模組 2＝路徑 A；模組 1、3、4、5＝路徑 B。","Per-module pre/post on that module’s items. Chain A and Chain B scores should not be summed.":"每個模組各自題目的前後測。路徑 A 與路徑 B 分數不應加總。","The live course, printable discussion prompts, and item bank. No cohort table.":"已上線課程、可列印討論提示與題庫；無群體結果表。","A bridge is an architecture. It is not proof that either chain produced learning. Live is not validated.":"橋梁是一種架構，不是任一條路徑已產生學習效果的證明。上線不等於驗證。","B1 · Odor Pixel Suite":"B1 · 氣味像素遊戲套組","Can a visitor treat a smell as a pattern across receptors, including mixtures — not as one private switch?":"訪客能否把氣味視為跨受體的模式，包含混合氣味，而不是一種氣味對應一個專用開關？","Adults and children; Junior–Challenge levels.":"成人與兒童；初階至挑戰難度。","Three browser games at":"三款瀏覽器遊戲位於",". Optional workshop study mode uses":"。選用的工作坊研究模式使用",". Everyday visitors are not quizzed.":"。一般訪客不需作答測驗。","Olfactory coding, pattern recognition, and mixture decoding. This is not the food-safety survey construct unless a future instrument is shown to use those items.":"嗅覺編碼、模式辨識與混合物解碼。除非未來工具證實使用了那些題目，否則這不是食品安全問卷所量測的構念。","Live (external hub)":"已上線（外部入口）","The live hub, documented learning objectives, and the suite’s educator pack. No playtest cohort, no paired rates.":"已上線入口、有文件記錄的學習目標與套組教育者教材包；無遊玩測試群體，也無配對比例。","A shipped game is not a published learning gain. Do not read game scores as mycotoxin-misconception correction.":"遊戲已發布不等於學習增益已發表。不要把遊戲分數解讀成真菌毒素迷思的修正。","B2 · Learning Lab Modules 1, 3, 4, and 5":"B2 · 學習實驗室模組 1、3、4、5","Can a visitor follow AeroSense from combinatorial smell, through a living sensor and a decoder, to a screening decision that is not a verdict?":"訪客能否沿著 AeroSense，從組合式嗅覺、活體感測器與解碼器，一路理解到「篩檢決策不是最終判定」？","Self-paced wiki visitors.":"自訂進度的 網站 訪客。",", each with its own three-item pre/post.":"，各自具有三題前後測。","Olfaction, heterologous sensing, pattern decoding, and responsible action language — Chain B concepts, not the three kitchen-safety claims.":"嗅覺、異源感測、模式解碼與負責任的行動用語：這些是路徑 B 概念，不是三項廚房安全說法。","Live modules. No published cohort.":"模組已上線；無已公布群體。","Unidentified visitors. Browser-local scores are not a sample.":"未識別身分的訪客；瀏覽器本機分數不是研究樣本。","B3 · Workshop / camp hands-on discussion":"B3 · 工作坊／營隊實作討論","Can students talk through and try this science with other people, not only click a page?":"學生能否與他人一起討論並嘗試這些科學，而不只是點擊頁面？","Planned university workshop with Prof. Chung-Chuan Lo; planned elementary-school camp.":"規劃與 Chung-Chuan Lo 教授合作的大學工作坊，以及國小營隊。","Hands-on session using the games and, where age-appropriate, Lab modules.":"使用遊戲的實作活動，並依年齡適切性加入學習實驗室模組。","Participation and facilitated discussion. Not a published dialogue record yet.":"參與與引導式討論；尚無已公布的對話記錄。","None. No quotes, photos, or attendance.":"無。沒有引言、照片或出席人數。","A planned conversation is not dialogue evidence.":"規劃中的對話，不是對話證據。","B4 · Conceptual / participation outcomes":"B4 · 概念／參與成果","After taking part, do students explain combinatorial smell, a living sensor, or screening-versus-verdict more carefully?":"參與後，學生能否更謹慎地解釋組合式嗅覺、活體感測器，以及篩檢與判定的區別？","Future workshop and camp cohorts.":"未來工作坊與營隊群體。","Planned conceptual and participation measures on Chain B ideas. Not the Chain A myth IDs unless that session actually uses them.":"規劃針對路徑 B 概念進行概念與參與量測。除非活動實際使用路徑 A 迷思 ID，否則不採用那些題目。","Nothing published. No outcome numbers are shown.":"尚無公布內容，不呈現成果數字。","None.":"無。","We do not invent conceptual-gain percentages. Chain B will not be reported as food-safety correction.":"我們不捏造概念增益百分比，也不將路徑 B 報告為食品安全觀念修正。","Why identical wording — and why that is not enough":"為何使用相同文字，以及為何仍然不夠","Benefit.":"優點。","On Chain A, Module 2 reuses the survey’s three statements with the same item IDs. That is for":"在路徑 A 中，模組 2 使用問卷相同的三個陳述與題目 ID，目的是","cross-instrument comparability":"跨工具可比性",": a diagnostic baseline and a later pre/post can be read against each other instead of against three unrelated quizzes.":"：讓診斷基準與後續前後測能相互對照，而不是比較三份毫無關聯的測驗。","Caution.":"注意。","Same-item pre/post testing can partly measure familiarity with the original sentence. If a future consented cohort is collected, we recommend one parallel “transfer” item per concept — a new wording of the same idea — to test whether learning generalizes. No transfer-item results exist, and none are shown.":"相同題目前後測可能部分量到對原始句子的熟悉度。若未來蒐集經同意的群體資料，我們建議每個概念加入一題平行「遷移」題，以不同措辭呈現相同概念，測試學習能否泛化。目前沒有遷移題結果，因此也未呈現任何結果。","Odor Pixel Suite is not in that wording match. Its teaching target is olfactory coding. Comparability across Chain A instruments does not license a combined “education impact” score with Chain B.":"氣味像素遊戲套組不屬於這組文字配對，其教學目標是嗅覺編碼。路徑 A 工具可比較，不代表可以與路徑 B 合併成「教育影響力」分數。","Iteration":"迭代","The right-hand column matters more than a generic outreach summary: what did evidence change in our education design?":"右欄比一般性的推廣摘要更重要：證據究竟改變了教育設計的什麼？","A completed arrow is shown only when a real redesign occurred. Internal design reviews are labeled as such. They are not participant quotes.":"只有實際發生重新設計，才顯示已完成的箭頭。內部設計審查會清楚標示，不當成參與者引言。","What learners may learn from us":"學習者可能從我們這裡學到什麼","Intended outcomes of live artifacts. These are teaching aims, not measured gains.":"已上線成果的預期成效。這些是教學目標，不是實測增益。","Track A.":"路線 A。","Reconsider the residual heat and look/smell food-safety claims (Module 2).":"重新思考仍存的加熱與外觀／氣味食品安全說法（模組 2）。","Track B.":"路線 B。","Treat odor as a pattern; see a living-sensor idea; interpret screening without treating it as a verdict (Lab 1, 3–5; Odor Pixel Suite).":"將氣味視為模式、理解活體感測器概念，並在解讀篩檢時不將其視為最終判定（學習實驗室 1、3–5；氣味像素遊戲套組）。","Participate.":"參與。","Planned workshop and camp. Not yet available.":"規劃中的工作坊與營隊，目前尚未提供。","What we learn from learners":"我們從學習者身上學到什麼","Documented education-design iterations only.":"僅列有記錄的教育設計迭代。","Evidence.":"證據。","Early n = 28 aggregate record":"早期 n = 28 彙整記錄",": 27/28 rejected the mold-removal claim, 24/28 the heat claim and 23/28 the look/smell claim. These are reported counts from the team narrative, not a reanalysis of a raw export.":"：27/28 否定移除黴菌的說法，24/28 否定加熱說法，23/28 否定外觀／氣味說法。這些是團隊敘述回報的人數，不是重新分析原始匯出檔的結果。","Change made.":"已做的改變。","Focused Track A on decision-related misconceptions instead of generic awareness.":"將路線 A 聚焦於與決策相關的迷思，而非一般性認知宣導。","Where it appears.":"出現位置。","This page;":"本頁；","; shared item IDs.":"；共享題目 ID。","Status.":"狀態。","Completed education-design iteration. Learning-gain evaluation still pending.":"已完成教育設計迭代；學習增益評估仍待進行。","Internal review after the games existed: odor-as-pattern play does not cover biology → engineering → computation → decision.":"遊戲完成後的內部審查：將氣味視為模式的遊戲，尚未涵蓋生物學 → 工程 → 運算 → 決策。","Interpretation.":"解讀。","A playable suite is not a full AeroSense pathway.":"可遊玩的套組，不等於完整 AeroSense 路徑。","Built the five-module Learning Lab alongside the games, with Module 2 matched to the survey items.":"在遊戲之外建立五模組學習實驗室，模組 2 與問卷題目對應。","Completed internal design iteration. Not a participant-feedback cycle.":"已完成內部設計迭代，不是參與者回饋循環。","Curriculum-writing constraint: a screening band is easy to read as a certificate.":"課程撰寫限制：篩檢分級容易被當成證明書。","Risk language can over-claim even when the science sentence is careful.":"即使科學敘述謹慎，風險用語仍可能過度宣稱。","Module 5 states that screening is not confirmatory testing and should trigger a next action, not a verdict.":"模組 5 明確說明，篩檢不是確認性檢測，應引導下一步行動，而不是作出最終判定。","Completed education-material change. Treating that sentence as a finished device UI is a separate, later evaluation — not claimed as a hardware redesign from this page.":"已完成教育材料修改。把這句話視為已完成的設備介面，屬於另一項較晚的評估；本頁不宣稱它已促成硬體重新設計。","No workshop, camp, or playtest export is published.":"尚未公布工作坊、營隊或遊玩測試的匯出資料。","Instruments can exist before audiences do.":"工具可以先於參與者群體存在。","None from participant feedback. The arrow stops here.":"尚無來自參與者回饋的改變；箭頭在此停止。","Where it would appear.":"未來會出現的位置。","Future Module / game copy, after a real export and notes.":"取得實際匯出資料與筆記後，更新模組／遊戲文案。","Education iteration model":"教育迭代模型","Assume":"假設","Completed. We assumed broad mold-risk misunderstanding.":"已完成。我們原本假設大眾普遍誤解黴菌風險。","Diagnose":"診斷","Completed. Initial survey.":"已完成。初期問卷。","Completed for current educational artifacts (two tracks, games, Lab, item IDs).":"目前教育成果已完成設計（兩條路線、遊戲、學習實驗室與題目 ID）。","Deliver":"交付","Games playable; Learning Lab live. Workshop and camp planned.":"遊戲可遊玩，學習實驗室已上線；工作坊與營隊規劃中。","Measure":"量測","Formal cohort evaluation pending.":"正式群體評估仍待進行。","Listen":"聆聽","Pending structured cohort feedback.":"等待有結構的群體回饋。","Revise":"修訂","Next evidence-based redesign pending.":"下一次依據證據的重新設計仍待進行。","Not just the lessons we built — but how someone else can run them.":"不只提供我們建立的課程，也說明其他人如何帶領。","Only resources that actually exist are listed. There is no Download button on a missing file. The linked game build, protocols and question bank are included in this wiki. Their published iGEM routes must be checked after deployment.":"僅列出實際存在的資源，不為缺失檔案放上下載按鈕。連結的遊戲版本、流程與題庫皆包含在此 網站 中；部署後仍須檢查其正式 iGEM 網址。","Resource manifest. Availability is a delivery fact. Evaluation status is separate.":"資源清單。可取得是交付事實，評估狀態另外呈現。","Resource":"資源","Format":"格式","Availability":"可用狀態","Reuse notes":"重用備註","Interactive olfactory-pattern education (three playable games)":"互動式嗅覺模式教育（三款可遊玩的遊戲）","General visitors; school / workshop learners":"一般訪客；學校／工作坊學習者","Browser suite":"瀏覽器遊戲套組","Live / playable":"已上線／可遊玩","· included in this wiki":"· 包含在此 網站 中","Next validation":"下一步驗證","Everyday visitors play immediately. Not official iGEM hosting yet.":"一般訪客可直接遊玩，目前尚非正式 iGEM 託管。","Suite educator record · includes archived Game 2":"套組教育者記錄 · 包含封存的遊戲 2","Educator overview and study workflow; QC Shift content is historical and does not describe the current Maze":"教育者概覽與研究流程；QC Shift 內容屬歷史記錄，不描述目前的迷宮","Facilitators":"活動帶領者","/education/":"/education/","Results empty":"結果空白","From PinChe567/iGEM-game. Game 2's QC Shift record is archived; no matched Maze outcome is available. Results fields stay empty until a real export.":"來自 PinChe567/iGEM-game。遊戲 2 的 QC Shift 記錄已封存，尚無相符的迷宮成果。在取得實際匯出資料前，結果欄位保持空白。","Education study protocol":"教育研究流程","Optional workshop study mode: paired pre/post, local export, how to count paired n":"選用工作坊研究模式：配對前後測、本機匯出，以及配對 n 的計算方式","Educators / research-style deployment":"教育工作者／研究形式的使用","Markdown":"Markdown","education-study-protocol.md":"education-study-protocol.md","Method documented; no cohort":"方法已記錄，尚無群體","Casual play does not use this protocol. Facilitators enable study mode; hub Play cards do not.":"一般遊玩不使用此流程。由活動帶領者啟用研究模式，入口的遊玩卡片不會啟用。","Question bank":"題庫","Conceptual item IDs and transfer items; G2 is archived QC Shift content":"概念題目 ID 與遷移應用題；G2 為封存的 QC Shift 內容","Facilitators analyzing exports":"分析匯出資料的活動帶領者","question-bank.md":"question-bank.md","No scored cohort":"無已評分群體","Traceable IDs. Do not recode answers to invent improvement.":"ID 可追溯。不要重新編碼答案以捏造進步。","Data dictionary / export schema":"資料字典／匯出綱要","Reproduce anonymous session fields, JSON/CSV export, paired-n rules":"重現匿名工作階段欄位、JSON／CSV 匯出與配對 n 規則","Facilitators / other iGEM teams":"活動帶領者／其他 iGEM 團隊","data-dictionary.md":"data-dictionary.md","Schema only":"僅有綱要","Storage key":"儲存鍵",". Empty cells mean missing, not zero. No PII fields.":"。空白欄位代表缺失，不是零；沒有個人識別資料欄位。","Playtest protocol":"遊玩測試流程","How to run a session and what not to collect":"如何執行一場活動，以及不應蒐集哪些資料","playtest-protocol.md":"playtest-protocol.md","Protocol; no filled session":"流程文件；尚無填妥的活動記錄","From PinChe567/iGEM-game":"來自 PinChe567/iGEM-game","Per-game facilitator notes":"各遊戲的帶領者筆記","Game-specific educator copy":"各遊戲專用的教育者說明","· pack":"· 教材包","Pending":"待完成","Files":"檔案",". Odor Maze (Scentbound Labyrinth) is the current Game 2.":"。氣味迷宮（Scentbound Labyrinth）是目前的遊戲 2。","and G2 question-bank items are archived QC Shift materials, not matched Maze teaching or assessment tools.":"與題庫 G2 題目，皆為封存的 QC Shift 教材，不是與目前迷宮相符的教學或評量工具。","Self-paced biology → engineering → decision curriculum":"自訂進度的生物學 → 工程 → 決策課程","Self-paced learners; educators":"自訂進度學習者；教育工作者","Wiki pages":"網站 頁面","Live on this wiki":"已在此 網站 上線","learning-platform.html":"learning-platform.html","Five modules, any order. Local store":"五個模組，可任意排序。本機儲存","Module 2 / survey item IDs":"模組 2／問卷題目 ID","Cross-instrument Track A comparison":"跨工具的路線 A 比較","Educators measuring food-safety claims":"量測食品安全說法的教育工作者","Live lesson +":"已上線課程＋","learning-02-mold.html":"learning-02-mold.html","IDs stable; no paired cohort":"ID 已固定；無配對群體","On-wiki discussion prompts":"網站 上的討論提示","Classroom talk after a module":"模組後的課堂討論","Educators":"教育工作者","HTML on the Lab":"學習實驗室中的 HTML","On-wiki":"網站 上提供","Learning Lab educator pack":"學習實驗室教育者教材包","Teaching aid, not dialogue evidence":"教學輔助，不是對話證據","Not a downloadable file. No Download button.":"不是可下載檔案，因此沒有下載按鈕。","Personal dashboard / local schema":"個人儀表板／本機資料綱要","Visitor can see their own pre/post in this browser":"訪客可在此瀏覽器查看自己的前後測","Self-paced learners":"自訂進度學習者","Wiki page + JS":"網站 頁面＋JS","progress.html":"progress.html","Not a study dataset":"不是研究資料集",". Nothing is sent until a consented backend exists.":"。在建立經同意的後端之前，不會傳送任何資料。","Teacher toolkit (guide, slides, worksheets)":"教師工具包（指南、投影片、學習單）","Printable classroom packet":"可列印的課堂教材包","Teachers":"教師","In preparation":"準備中","· no file":"· 尚無檔案","No placeholder download. See":"不提供占位下載。詳見","Reusable graphics / QR pack":"可重用圖像／QR 碼套件","Screenshots, GIFs, QR codes":"截圖、GIF、QR 碼","Wiki / classroom":"網站／課堂","Not in this repository":"此儲存庫未提供","Do not invent paths.":"不捏造檔案路徑。","For educators: optional study mode":"給教育工作者：選用研究模式","Casual visitors play the suite immediately. There is no mandatory pre-test on the public Play path. That is the default learner experience.":"一般訪客可直接遊玩套組。公開遊玩路徑沒有強制前測；這是預設的學習者體驗。","A separate workshop study mode can add paired measurement. For Game 2, the archived QC Shift G2 items do not match the current maze; they must not be interpreted as a Maze learning-gain measure. A matched Maze protocol remains to be developed. Facilitators follow the":"另設的工作坊研究模式可加入配對量測。對遊戲 2 而言，封存的 QC Shift G2 題目與目前迷宮不符，不得解讀為迷宮學習增益量測。相符的迷宮流程仍待開發。活動帶領者依照","education study protocol":"教育研究流程",": two short pre questions, the usual game, the same concepts after play plus one transfer item, optional feedback, then anonymous JSON (source of truth) and optional CSV. Answers stay in that browser. Nothing is transmitted automatically.":"：兩題簡短前測、一般遊戲、遊玩後測試相同概念並增加一題遷移應用題、選用回饋，再匯出匿名 JSON（主要依據）與選用 CSV。答案保留在該瀏覽器，不會自動傳送。","How to turn the mode on is documented in that protocol, not as this page’s primary play button.":"如何開啟此模式，記錄在該流程中，而不是本頁的主要遊玩按鈕。","View educator resources":"查看教育者資源","Run this yourself":"自己帶領活動","A reproducible workflow for another team. Casual game play does not require steps 4–8. The evaluation workflow is optional for educators and workshops.":"供其他團隊重現的流程。一般遊玩不需要步驟 4–8；評估流程是教育工作者與工作坊的選用項目。","Choose the audience (general public, elementary, university, self-paced).":"選擇對象（一般大眾、國小、大學、自訂進度學習者）。","Define the learning objective (Track A decision claims, or Track B olfactory / synbio ideas — not both as one score).":"定義學習目標（路線 A 的決策說法，或路線 B 的嗅覺／合成生物學概念；不將兩者合為一個分數）。","Select the relevant Learning Lab module and/or Odor Pixel game.":"選擇相關的學習實驗室模組及／或 Odor Pixel 遊戲。","If evaluation is intended, administer the pre-instrument (Lab quiz, or game study mode).":"若要進行評估，先施測前測工具（學習實驗室測驗或遊戲研究模式）。","Run the activity.":"進行活動。","Administer the paired post-instrument.":"施測配對後測工具。","Match responses using the documented anonymous / item-ID workflow. Paired":"依文件所述的匿名／題目 ID 流程配對回覆。配對","counts only sessions with scored pre and post for the same ID. Do not impute missing posts.":"僅計入同一 ID 同時有可計分前測與後測的工作階段。不補值缺失的後測。","Report exact denominators and limitations. Empty is not zero.":"報告確切分母與限制。空白不是零。","Collect qualitative feedback separately from anonymous JSON. Do not merge with class lists.":"質性回饋與匿名 JSON 分開蒐集，不與班級名冊合併。","Change the educational material only if evidence supports a redesign, and log it.":"只有在證據支持重新設計時，才修改教育材料，並留下記錄。","Why shared item IDs — and why that is not enough":"為何共享題目 ID，以及為何仍然不夠","See":"詳見","for the same-item / transfer caution. Game study mode already includes transfer IDs; no transfer-item results are reported here.":"關於相同題目／遷移應用的注意事項。遊戲研究模式已包含遷移題 ID；此處未報告遷移題結果。","Teach it yourself":"自己教學","Conference poster · PDF":"研討會海報 · PDF","Facilitator study guide":"活動帶領者研究指南","Export dictionary":"匯出資料字典","Discussion prompts":"討論提示","Early survey aggregates":"早期問卷彙整","A dedicated slide deck, print-and-play adaptation, original survey form and packaged teacher worksheets are not yet available. The live Module 2 items reproduce the three diagnostic claims; they do not replace the original four-module survey instrument. Wiki-authored content follows the site’s CC BY 4.0 notice; third-party assets and game software retain their own notices.":"專用投影片、列印遊玩改編版、原始問卷及套裝教師學習單，目前尚未提供。已上線模組 2 題目重現三項診斷說法，但不能取代原始四模組問卷工具。網站 原創內容遵循網站的 CC BY 4.0 聲明；第三方素材與遊戲軟體保留各自的授權聲明。","Limits":"限制","These are the bounds of the claim, not an apology for building the tools.":"這些界定的是主張範圍，不是為建立工具而致歉。","Initial survey sample caveats and item-level analysis status:":"初期問卷樣本注意事項與逐題分析狀態：",". Not a population prevalence or learning-gain study.":"。這不是人口盛行比例或學習增益研究。","Exact-item pre/post may create familiarity effects. Transfer-item results are not available — see":"完全相同題目的前後測可能產生熟悉效應。遷移題結果尚未取得；詳見","measurement caution":"量測注意事項","An immediate post-test, when it exists, will not establish long-term retention.":"即使未來有立即後測，也不能確立長期保留效果。","Social engagement does not establish learning. Reach figures are not reported yet.":"社群互動不能證明學習；觸及數據尚未報告。","Live Odor Pixel Suite / Learning Lab ≠ educational effectiveness. The second game is Odor Maze (Scentbound Labyrinth). The archived QC Shift guide and G2 questions do not assess the current maze.":"氣味像素遊戲套組／學習實驗室已上線，不等於具有教育成效。第二款遊戲是氣味迷宮（Scentbound Labyrinth）；封存的 QC Shift 指南與 G2 題目，不評估目前的迷宮。","Planned workshop and camp cannot yet provide outcome evidence. Different age groups will not be pooled as one equivalent cohort.":"規劃中的工作坊與營隊尚不能提供成果證據。不同年齡組別，不會合併為一個等效群體。","Survey and Module 2 share food-safety items; games teach olfactory coding / mixture decoding. We will not report a single correction rate across instruments unless items actually match.":"問卷與模組 2 共用食品安全題目；遊戲則教嗅覺編碼／混合物解碼。除非題目確實相符，否則不會跨工具報告單一答題修正率。","This Education wiki page provides fixed English and Traditional Chinese translations. The game suite is bilingual (zh-Hant / English). No separate bilingual teacher packet is published on this wiki.":"本教育 網站 頁面提供固定的英文與繁體中文譯文。遊戲套組為雙語（繁體中文／英文）。此 網站 尚未發布獨立的雙語教師教材包。","The next delivery round brings the existing materials to facilitated audiences, then evaluates paired responses and a transfer question. Attendance, consent arrangements, versioned materials and exact paired denominators will accompany any outcome claim. Recovering the original survey export and verifying the later 107-response total remain separate tasks.":"下一輪交付會將既有教材帶到有引導的觀眾群體，再評估配對回覆與一題遷移應用題。任何成果主張都會附上出席記錄、同意安排、具版本的教材與確切配對分母。找回原始問卷匯出檔，以及核實後期 107 份回覆總數，仍是獨立工作。","Planned · Xinfeng, Hsinchu":"規劃中 · 新竹新豐","For younger learners, we plan shorter concepts, visual comparisons and guided play. The aim is to help a child explain how a pattern can carry information and why a result can still be uncertain.":"對年幼學習者，我們規劃更簡短的概念、視覺比較與引導式遊玩。目標是幫助孩子解釋模式如何攜帶資訊，以及為何結果仍可能不確定。","The current plan identifies Xinfeng, Hsinchu. A confirmed activity record, attendance, photographs and learning outcomes are still to be added. Participation and any photographs will follow school and guardian arrangements.":"目前規劃地點為新竹新豐。已確認的活動記錄、出席人數、照片與學習成果仍待補入。參與及任何照片使用，皆將遵循學校與監護人的安排。","Planned · with Prof. Chung-Chuan Lo":"規劃中 · 與 Chung-Chuan Lo 教授合作","Computational neuroscience workshop":"計算神經科學工作坊","For high-school-to-university learners, the planned workshop moves from biological inspiration to model reasoning. Participants will connect an odor-response pattern to coding, noise and a classifier's limits, using the curriculum and games as discussion material.":"面向高中至大學學習者的規劃工作坊，將從生物靈感走向模型推理。參與者會以課程與遊戲作為討論材料，將氣味反應模式連結至編碼、雜訊與分類器的限制。","The format is planned with Prof. Chung-Chuan Lo. A completed workshop and measured learning effect are not yet part of this record.":"活動形式正與 Chung-Chuan Lo 教授共同規劃。已完成的工作坊與實測學習效果，尚未納入此記錄。","The next technical carousels, short science videos and printable teacher packet will follow the same assessment map. No effect is inferred from a published activity alone.":"下一批技術輪播圖、科學短影片與可列印教師教材包，都將依循同一評量地圖。不會僅憑活動已發布，就推論其效果。","Three stages of the education journey":"教育旅程的三個階段","Survey limitation":"問卷限制","Open full-size image: AeroSense Instagram educational carousel explaining the living odor-sensor concept.":"開啟完整尺寸影像：AeroSense Instagram 教育輪播圖，解釋活體氣味感測器概念。","AeroSense Instagram educational carousel explaining the living odor-sensor concept.":"AeroSense Instagram 教育輪播圖，解釋活體氣味感測器概念。","Open full-size image: A second graphic from the AeroSense Parts Design Instagram teaching carousel.":"開啟完整尺寸影像：AeroSense 元件設計 Instagram 教學輪播圖的第二張圖。","A second graphic from the AeroSense Parts Design Instagram teaching carousel.":"AeroSense 元件設計 Instagram 教學輪播圖的第二張圖。","Open full-size image: AeroSense team at the SynBioBeta 2026 poster presentation.":"開啟完整尺寸影像：AeroSense 團隊於 SynBioBeta 2026 海報展示。","AeroSense team at the SynBioBeta 2026 poster presentation.":"AeroSense 團隊於 SynBioBeta 2026 海報展示。","Open full-size image: Team photograph from SynBioBeta 2026.":"開啟完整尺寸影像：SynBioBeta 2026 團隊合照。","Team photograph from SynBioBeta 2026.":"SynBioBeta 2026 團隊合照。","Open full-size image: AeroSense guest lecture in a neuroscience course at China Medical University.":"開啟完整尺寸影像：AeroSense 於中國醫藥大學神經科學課程的客座演講。","AeroSense guest lecture in a neuroscience course at China Medical University.":"AeroSense 於中國醫藥大學神經科學課程的客座演講。","Open full-size image: Students and presenters during the China Medical University session.":"開啟完整尺寸影像：中國醫藥大學課程中的學生與講者。","Students and presenters during the China Medical University session.":"中國醫藥大學課程中的學生與講者。","Learning objectives, activities and assessment":"學習目標、活動與評量","Delivery versus evaluation":"交付與評估的區別","Assume, diagnose, design, deliver, measure, listen, revise":"假設、診斷、設計、交付、量測、聆聽、修訂","Reusable education resource manifest":"可重用教育資源清單","Education · AeroSense · NTHU iGEM 2026":"教育 · AeroSense · NTHU iGEM 2026","From curiosity to informed decisions":"從好奇到有依據的決策","Practise the decision":"練習做決策","Our early survey redirected teaching from general mold awareness to decisions about heat, smell and visible spoilage. We built activities in which learners choose, receive an explanation and apply the idea again. The redesign used 28 responses; the later reported total of 107 still lacks verified item-level counts.":"早期問卷讓教學從黴菌的一般知識，轉向加熱、氣味與可見腐敗的判斷。我們設計了讓學習者選擇、閱讀解釋並再次應用的活動。這次改版依據 28 份回覆；後續回報的 107 份尚缺經核對的逐題統計。","Start with familiar choices":"從熟悉的選擇出發","Survey findings shaped the lessons":"問卷發現引導教學","Two collection stages":"兩階段問卷","Sample limitations":"樣本限制","Three browser games make odor patterns tangible through recognition, navigation and mixture decoding. These simplified models invite learners to test their intuition; formal learning evaluation is pending.":"三款瀏覽器遊戲透過辨識、導航與混合氣味解碼，讓氣味模式變得具體。學習者可在簡化模型中檢驗直覺；正式學習成效仍待評估。","Science in a social feed":"社群裡的科學","Instagram introduces the project through technical carousels, sustainability questions and short explanations. Each format connects one scientific idea to a familiar decision.":"Instagram 透過技術輪播、永續提問與簡短說明介紹專題，每種形式都將一個科學概念連結到熟悉的決策。","Connect the concepts":"串起核心概念","Learn through dialogue":"透過對話學習","Industry audiences, neuroscience students and other iGEM teams challenged different parts of our explanation. These exchanges helped us refine the story; they were not controlled learning trials.":"產業聽眾、神經科學學生與其他 iGEM 隊伍，分別挑戰了說明中的不同環節。交流協助我們修正敘事，但並非受控的學習成效試驗。","SynBioBeta exchange":"SynBioBeta 交流","Biology before engineering":"從生物原理理解工程","Learning across teams":"跨隊伍交流","Resources others can reuse":"可供他人再用的資源","Evaluate learning":"評估學習成效","Current evidence":"現有證據","Paired learning-gain evaluation is pending.":"配對學習成效評估尚待完成。","Reach measures exposure; learning requires assessment.":"觸及呈現接觸程度；學習成效需要評量。","Two assessment pathways":"兩條評量路徑","Each node identifies the delivered activity and its evaluation status.":"每個節點標明已提供的活動及其評估狀態。","Comparability and transfer":"可比性與知識遷移","Shared assessment items":"共用評量題目","What changed in our teaching":"教學如何改變","The record below links each piece of evidence to a teaching decision.":"以下紀錄將每項證據連結到具體教學決策。","Teach with AeroSense":"用 AeroSense 教學","Use the lessons, games and evaluation protocol in your own setting.":"將課程、遊戲及評估程序運用於自己的教學情境。","The game build, protocols and question bank are included in this wiki. The packaged teacher toolkit is still in preparation.":"本 wiki 已收錄遊戲、程序與題庫；整套教師工具包仍在準備中。","Evaluation limits":"評估限制","The resources are available; their effect on learning still requires a documented evaluation.":"教學資源已可使用，學習效果仍需有紀錄的評估。","Next: evaluate with learners":"下一步：與學習者共同評估","Our 28-response survey redirected teaching from general mold awareness to decisions about heat, smell and visible spoilage. Learners make a choice, examine the reasoning and apply the idea again.":"28 份問卷回覆使教學從一般黴菌認知，轉向加熱、氣味與可見腐敗的判斷。學習者先做選擇、檢視推理，再應用概念。","Active learning informed our approach. Freeman and colleagues synthesized 225 undergraduate STEM studies and reported an average 0.47-standard-deviation examination improvement. Wouters and colleagues found benefits of serious games for learning and retention.":"主動學習研究提供設計依據。Freeman 等人彙整 225 項大學 STEM 研究，報告考試表現平均提升 0.47 個標準差；Wouters 等人則發現嚴肅遊戲有助於學習與保留。","Choose an answer, read the reasoning and reconsider your decision. Choices remain in this browser tab.":"選擇答案、閱讀推理，再檢視自己的判斷。選擇保留在此瀏覽器分頁中。","The 23 August 2026 record contains 28 responses. Most respondents rejected all three claims, so we focused teaching on applying those ideas to food decisions.":"2026 年 8 月 23 日的記錄含 28 份回覆。多數受訪者否定三項說法，因此教學聚焦於如何把概念運用在食物判斷上。","The table reports aggregate counts from a convenience sample and guided curriculum design. Percentages use the stated denominators.":"表格呈現便利樣本的彙整計數，用於課程設計；百分比依列出的分母計算。","Three browser games teach odor patterns through recognition, navigation and mixture decoding.":"三款瀏覽器遊戲透過辨識、導航與混合物解碼，介紹氣味模式。","The first carousel follows an odor signal through the receptor, calcium entry and fluorescent reporter. The two published graphics introduce the receptor and reporter designs.":"第一組輪播圖沿著受體、鈣離子流入與螢光報導蛋白追蹤氣味訊號。兩張已發布圖解介紹受體與報導蛋白設計。","Each module includes a short assessment and personal feedback stored in the learner’s browser.":"每個模組包含簡短評量，個人回饋儲存在學習者的瀏覽器。","Industry audiences, neuroscience students and other iGEM teams helped us refine how we explain the project.":"業界觀眾、神經科學學生與其他 iGEM 隊伍協助我們改進專案說明。","The Learning Lab, browser games and educator protocol are available for reuse below.":"以下提供可重用的 Learning Lab、瀏覽器遊戲及教育者操作方法。","Use the same anonymous session and instrument for paired pre/post comparisons. Analyze food-safety decisions and olfactory-coding scores separately.":"前後測配對須使用同一匿名工作階段及評量工具；食安判斷與嗅覺編碼分數分開分析。","The curriculum uses two assessment chains: food-safety decisions and olfactory literacy. Shared item IDs connect equivalent questions within each chain.":"課程分為食安判斷與嗅覺素養兩條評量路徑；同一路徑內，以共用題目編號連結等同問題。","Module 2 belongs to Chain A; Modules 1, 3, 4 and 5 belong to Chain B.":"模組 2 屬於路徑 A；模組 1、3、4、5 屬於路徑 B。","Optional study mode pairs pre/post items and a transfer question, then exports anonymous JSON or CSV locally. The archived QC Shift G2 items apply to QC Shift; the current Maze has different learning objectives.":"選用研究模式可配對前後測與遷移題，並在本機匯出匿名 JSON 或 CSV。封存的 QC Shift G2 題目適用於 QC Shift；目前的迷宮遊戲有不同學習目標。","Educators can reproduce the optional evaluation workflow below.":"教育者可依下列步驟重現選用的評量流程。","Report paired-response counts and missing responses.":"報告配對回覆數與缺失回覆。","The 28-response survey found 27/28 rejected the mold-removal claim, 24/28 the heating claim and 23/28 the look-and-smell claim. We used those decisions to focus Module 2 and reuse the same item IDs.":"28 份回覆中，27/28 否定去除黴菌即可安全食用、24/28 否定加熱即可去除風險、23/28 否定外觀與氣味正常即安全。我們據此聚焦模組 2，並沿用相同題目編號。","An internal review identified a gap between odor-pattern games and the complete sensing system. We built the five-module Learning Lab to connect biology, engineering, computation and decisions.":"內部檢視發現，氣味模式遊戲尚未涵蓋完整感測系統。我們建立五模組 Learning Lab，串起生物、工程、運算與決策。","We revised Module 5 around the action following a screening result: monitor, retest or escalate to confirmation.":"我們將模組 5 聚焦於篩檢結果之後的行動：監測、複測或進行確認檢測。","The diagnostic record contains 28 responses and three aggregate item counts.":"診斷性問卷記錄含 28 份回覆及三項彙整計數。","Shared item IDs connect equivalent questions across the survey and Module 2.":"共用題目編號連結問卷與模組 2 的等同問題。","Select an activity to inspect its teaching method and reusable materials.":"選擇活動，查看教學方法與可重用教材。","Facilitator guide":"帶領者指南","Stable item IDs support traceable scoring.":"固定題目編號支援可追溯計分。","Discussion prompts are available within the Learning Lab.":"討論提示位於 Learning Lab 中。","Scores and reflections stay in the visitor’s browser.":"分數與反思保留在使用者的瀏覽器中。","Learning goals":"學習目標","You disagreed. Correct. The explanation below shows why.":"你選擇不同意，答對了。下方說明解釋原因。","You agreed. Reconsider this claim using the explanation below.":"你選擇同意。請閱讀下方說明，再想一想這個說法。"});
